references/dispatch-reference.md:1:# SDD Dispatch Reference — codex / opencode / agy
references/dispatch-reference.md:3:> Living document. Every fact is stamped with the CLI version it was verified against.
references/dispatch-reference.md:4:> If the installed version differs, re-run the [verification protocol](verification-protocol.md) before trusting this page.
references/dispatch-reference.md:6:## Cross-CLI comparison (the one-glance table)
references/dispatch-reference.md:10:| Prompt argument | positional (or stdin) | **positional** (`-p` = basic-auth *password*!) | `-p "<PROMPT>"` — **must be last arg** |
references/dispatch-reference.md:14:| Exit codes | Normal 0/1 | Normal 0/1 | Normal 0/1 (≥1.1.4; earlier versions reportedly returned 1 on success) |
references/dispatch-reference.md:15:| Model validation | **Server-side** — bogus → HTTP 400, exit 1 | Errors (JSON) on bogus model, exit 1 | Errors cleanly, lists available models |
references/dispatch-reference.md:16:| Reasoning-effort control | `-c model_reasoning_effort=<low…max>` — **validated** (bogus → 400) | `--variant <high\|max\|minimal…>` — **silently ignored if unsupported** | Effort-in-name (`-low/-medium/-high` slug or `(Low)` label) **or** base slug + `--effort` — mixing both **errors** |
references/dispatch-reference.md:17:| Output contract | stdout + `-o <file>` = **last message only** | Clean stdout (small `build · model` banner) | stdout, **but** document tasks divert to brain files (see gotchas) |
